    overview: "Ecuador is one of South America's most diverse and affordable countries — a nation that packs the Amazon rainforest, Andean highlands, Pacific coast beaches, and the legendary Galápagos Islands into a relatively compact territory. It uses the US dollar (no currency risk), has one of the most accessible retirement visa programs globally, and Cuenca is internationally famous as the world's best retirement city. Quito, the capital, sits at 2,850m — giving it an eternal spring climate.",
